//max sum subarray of size k


interview- First, I will calculate the sum of the first K elements because I need to find the maximum sum of a subarray of size K.

After calculating the first window sum, I will store it in a variable called ans.

Now, instead of calculating the sum again for every window, I will use the Sliding Window technique.

I will move the window one position to the right. For that, I will subtract the element that is leaving the window and add the new element that is entering the window.

After every movement, I will update the maximum sum.

I will repeat this until I reach the last window, and finally return the maximum sum.

class Solution{
  public:
    long maxSubarraySum(vector<int>& Arr, int K){
        int n=Arr.size();
        int low=0;
        int high=K-1;
        int sum=0;
        for(int i=0;i<=high;i++){
             sum+=Arr[i];
        }
        int ans=sum;
        while(high<n-1){          // If you are doing high++ inside the loop, then the condition should usually be this otherwise it <= will go out of bound
            low++;
            high++;
            sum=sum-Arr[low-1]+Arr[high];
            ans=max(ans,sum);
        }
        return ans;
    }
};
